        <mxCell id="g8" value="Yes" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;jettySize=auto;orthogonalLoop=1;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#E6E6E6;" edge="1" parent="1" source="d5" target="n32"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="g9" value="No:&lt;br&gt;roll back" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;jettySize=auto;orthogonalLoop=1;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#E6E6E6;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=1;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="d5" target="n31"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="l8" value="re-Update Shared WS&lt;br&gt;to the restored state,&lt;br&gt;then re-promote" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;jettySize=auto;orthogonalLoop=1;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#E6E6E6;dashed=1;strokeColor=#8c8c8c;fontColor=#4d4d4d;exitX=1;exitY=0.4;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.25;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n31" target="n20"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as='points'><mxPoint x="1180" y="3602"/><mxPoint x="1180" y="2080"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="l9" value="re-work the defect on&lt;br&gt;a fresh feature branch" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;jettySize=auto;orthogonalLoop=1;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#E6E6E6;dashed=1;strokeColor=#8c8c8c;fontColor=#4d4d4d;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.7;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n31" target="n9"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as='points'><mxPoint x="770" y="3613"/><mxPoint x="770" y="316"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e28" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;jettySize=auto;orthogonalLoop=1;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#E6E6E6;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n32" target="n33"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="g10" value="hand-off" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;jettySize=auto;orthogonalLoop=1;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#E6E6E6;dashed=1;strokeColor=#8c8c8c;fontColor=#4d4d4d;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n32" target="offpage"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e29" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;jettySize=auto;orthogonalLoop=1;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#E6E6E6;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n33" target="end"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="l10" value="Feedback → backlog&lt;br&gt;(next iteration)" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;jettySize=auto;orthogonalLoop=1;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#E6E6E6;dashed=1;strokeColor=#8c8c8c;fontColor=#4d4d4d;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.9;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n33" target="n9"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as='points'><mxPoint x="745" y="3840"/><mxPoint x="745" y="335"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="legendBox" value="Legend — Operational Domain" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=4;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="80" y="1560" width="560" height="175" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="leg0" value="CC / VSC on Local Files" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=9;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" vertex="1" parent="legendBox"><mxGeometry x="15" y="40" width="250" height="28" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="leg1" value="CC via MCP against Fabric" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=9;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" vertex="1" parent="legendBox"><mxGeometry x="290" y="40" width="250" height="28" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="leg2" value="Fabric Web UI — sole activity surface" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=9;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;" vertex="1" parent="legendBox"><mxGeometry x="15" y="76" width="250" height="28" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="leg3" value="Local Git / Mixed (Git · ADO · Fabric · CC)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=9;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" vertex="1" parent="legendBox"><mxGeometry x="290" y="76" width="250" height="28" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="leg4" value="Azure DevOps (ADO) — sole activity surface" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=9;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;" vertex="1" parent="legendBox"><mxGeometry x="15" y="112" width="250" height="28" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="leg5" value="Decision Gateway" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=9;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;" vertex="1" parent="legendBox"><mxGeometry x="290" y="112" width="250" height="28" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="legPhase" value="Solid dark-grey border = phase boundary · dashed grey arrow = feedback / rollback path" style="text;html=1;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="legendBox"><mxGeometry x="15" y="146" width="530" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="abbrevBox" value="Key — Abbreviations" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=4;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="80" y="1780" width="560" height="240" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="abbrevL" value="ADO — Azure DevOps&lt;br&gt;ADR — Architecture Decision Record&lt;br&gt;API — Application Programming Interface&lt;br&gt;CC — Claude Code (CLI)&lt;br&gt;CLI — Command-Line Interface&lt;br&gt;Ctx — Context: active Fabric WS / Git branch&lt;br&gt;DAX — Data Analysis Expressions&lt;br&gt;Fab — Fabric (commit-message prefix)&lt;br&gt;JSON — JavaScript Object Notation&lt;br&gt;MCP — Model Context Protocol&lt;br&gt;OLS — Object-Level Security&lt;br&gt;PR — Pull Request" style="text;html=1;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;spacingLeft=4;" vertex="1" parent="abbrevBox"><mxGeometry x="12" y="34" width="268" height="196" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="abbrevR" value="QA — Quality Assurance&lt;br&gt;RBAC — Role-Based Access Control&lt;br&gt;REST — Representational State Transfer&lt;br&gt;RLS — Row-Level Security&lt;br&gt;SC — Source Control (Fabric panel)&lt;br&gt;SDLC — Software Development Life Cycle&lt;br&gt;SHA — Secure Hash Algorithm (commit hash)&lt;br&gt;SQL — Structured Query Language&lt;br&gt;T-SQL — Transact-SQL&lt;br&gt;TMDL — Tabular Model Definition Language&lt;br&gt;VSC — Visual Studio Code&lt;br&gt;WS — Workspace" style="text;html=1;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;spacingLeft=4;" vertex="1" parent="abbrevBox"><mxGeometry x="290" y="34" width="258" height="196" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="notesBox" value="Notes (cited in steps as ᵃ ᵇ ᶜ …; letter q omitted — no superscript form)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=4;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="80" y="2050" width="560" height="1720" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="notesText" value="&lt;b&gt;a&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; — Specs as versioned artifacts: ADRs, source-to-target mappings, measure definitions and pipeline specs are Markdown in the repo, drafted from reusable CC CLI templates and merged in the same PR as the code they describe. Step 1 is one-off inception; Step 9 is the recurring re-entry point, and all feedback and defect loops return there.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;b&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; — Branch strategy: main + short-lived feature branches only. No test/prod branches — Test/Prod content is delivered by Deployment Pipelines, not Git; Git binding applies only to Dev-stage workspaces.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;c&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; — Shared Integration/Dev WS: bound to main, doubling as the Deployment Pipeline Dev stage. Personal Dev WSs are branched workspaces outside the pipeline.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;d&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; — Branch out: Fabric’s “Branch out to new workspace” creates the branch and the bound workspace together — no pre-created local branch. Item definitions are copied; data and bindings are not. Lakehouses and warehouses arrive empty, so repoint sources at the Personal WS (note ʸ), re-create shortcuts (note ᵗ) and run the ingestion pipelines (Step 16) before validating.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;e&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; — No auto-commit: Fabric Git Integration never commits automatically; a manual Source Control → Commit is always required.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;f&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; — Sync rule: local edits are invisible to Fabric until pushed to ADO and pulled via workspace “Update”. MCP always operates on workspace state, never local files.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;g&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; — Commit/PR message body: [domain]_[artifact]_[action]; PRs merge feature → main with peer review.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;h&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; — Automation candidate: the manual workspace “Update” at Steps 15 and 20 is a single-owner action today; automatable via the Fabric Git REST API.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;i&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; — Deployment Pipelines — one-off setup (outside the release loop): create the pipeline, assign the Dev/Test/Prod workspaces to stages. Per release, pipelines copy item structure and metadata only; data does not deploy. Standing rule: what the pipeline does not copy it also does not clear, so it persists once set — endorsement (note ᵖ), RBAC and RLS membership (note ʷ), bindings and credentials (note ʸ) are first-release / on-change actions, never per-promotion. Environment-specific values come from the Variable Library (note ᵘ); Deployment Rules are the fallback.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;j&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; — Report hand-off: reports are authored in the Fabric Web UI against the endorsed Prod semantic model and stored in the Prod WS. That SDLC is out of scope here.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;k&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; — Release tag: tag the exact commit deployed to Test, not the newest commit on main, which may have moved on. Because the Prod WS is not Git-bound, the last successfully verified tag — not necessarily the newest — is the authoritative record of what is in Prod and the reference point a rollback restores main to (note ˣ). A tag whose release was rolled back stays on main as history; the fix ships under a new tag. Reserve scripted git tag / push --tags for release automation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;l&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; — Commit prefixes by surface: local VSC: “VSC Commit: ” · local CC: “CC Commit: ” · ADO web: “ADO Commit: ” · Fabric UI: “Fab Commit: ”. Body follows note ᵍ.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;m&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; — Rollback on main: if merged changes fail integration validation, restore main rather than fixing forward on a broken main. Revert, never reset (rationale in note ˣ): in ADO, Revert the merged PR (git revert -m 1 &amp;lt;merge-SHA&amp;gt;) and complete the revert PR. Both outcome edges always fire.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;n&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; — Pre-PR sync: fetch and merge (or rebase onto) main, resolving conflicts locally in VSC — TMDL and pipeline JSON must be resolved as text, since Fabric cannot. The merged result has never run anywhere, so Step 18 returns to Step 15 for re-validation. The gateway releases the branch only once it is in sync, catching main moving again during re-validation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;o&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; — Cleanup: after a validated merge, delete the feature branch in ADO and delete or unbind the Personal Dev WS, preventing orphaned workspaces and stale bindings.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;p&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; — Endorsement: promotion / certification is item metadata the pipeline neither copies nor clears (note ⁱ), so an endorsed model stays endorsed across promotions. Step 32 applies it on first release, repeated only when the level is deliberately changed or withdrawn. Certification requires a tenant-designated certifier.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;r&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; — MCP write rule: MCP acts on workspace state, so anything it creates bypasses Git and PR review until manually committed in Fabric, leaving repo/workspace drift invisible. Standing rule: MCP is run / read / validate only (Steps 16, 17, 21, 30, 33), from the servers registered at Step 4. Item definitions are authored locally as TMDL, T-SQL and pipeline JSON (Step 13) and reach Fabric via Git; Step 5 is the sole exception, seeding an empty repo with empty shells.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;s&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; — Plan Mode: CC plan mode proposes an implementation plan without writing to disk, so intent is agreed before code exists. No local authoring begins until approval; the approved plan is committed into the spec set (note ᵃ).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;t&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; — Connections &amp;amp; shortcuts: source connections, gateways and OneLake shortcuts are workspace/tenant-level objects, created at Step 6 once the shells they attach to exist — a shortcut cannot precede its lakehouse. Not versioned in Git, and carried neither by Deployment Pipelines nor by branch-out: every pipeline stage and every branched Personal Dev WS needs its own. Binding an item to them is separate (note ʸ).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;u&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; — Variable Library: a first-class, Git-versioned Fabric item holding environment-specific values (lakehouse IDs, connection references, parameters) as named value sets. Scaffold it with the other shells at Step 5, one set per stage; each stage activates its own, so no hard-coded IDs travel between Dev, Test and Prod. The active set is stage configuration, not part of the item definition, so deployment does not overwrite it — confirm it at each promotion.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;v&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; — RLS / OLS: row- and object-level security roles are part of the semantic model definition and live in TMDL, so they are authored, committed and PR-reviewed like any other code (Step 13) and tested with “View as role” before the PR. Role membership is separate, assigned per workspace (note ʷ).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;w&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; — Capacity &amp;amp; access. Capacity is infrastructure: the three deployment-pipeline workspaces (Shared Integration/Dev, Test, Prod) are bound to a Fabric capacity (F-SKU or trial) at Step 3, and the branched Personal Dev WSs created at Step 10 need capacity at creation too — without it Spark and Direct Lake will not work in any workspace, and the pipeline will not deploy across the three stages. Access is identity: RLS membership cannot be granted against a model that does not yet exist in Prod, so Step 29 follows the promotion. RBAC and RLS membership both persist (note ⁱ), making Step 29 a first-release and roster-change action.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;x&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; — Prod verification &amp;amp; rollback: Fabric has no one-click Prod rollback. If verification fails, restore main by reverting, never resetting — a reset rewrites shared, PR-protected history and needs a force push. In ADO, revert the PR(s) merged since the previous release tag (note ᵏ), newest first, so main is restored by new commits. The failed tag is left in place and the previous verified tag becomes the Prod record (note ᵏ). Recovery is a full re-Update and re-promotion cycle; both outcome edges always fire.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;y&lt;/b&gt;&amp;#160; — Bindings &amp;amp; credentials: pipelines copy item definitions, not connections — and neither does branch-out. A newly deployed or newly branched item is unbound and holds no credentials, so the model cannot refresh until both are set on its settings page. Later deployments do not reset them (note ⁱ), making Steps 25 and 28 first-release and rebind-on-change actions; the same rebind applies in the Personal Dev WS at Step 10 (note ᵈ). Direct Lake models never autobind and always need an explicit rule or manual rebind." style="text;html=1;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="notesBox"><mxGeometry x="10" y="36" width="540" height="1670" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
